<title>USA: U.S. June housing starts rose 4.8 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. June housing starts rose 4.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce housing starts and</p>
<p>building permits, seasonally adjusted annual rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p> PCT CHANGE:June     May (Prev)     Apr (Prev)  June97/96</p>
<p> -Starts     4.8    -6.6   -4.8     0.3   -0.7	 -2.4</p>
<p> -Permits   -2.6    -0.7    0.1    -1.0   -1.0	 -2.6</p>
<p> RATES	June     May (Prev)     Apr (Prev)  June 1996</p>
<p> -Starts   1,452   1,385  1,397   1,483  1,468	1,488</p>
<p> -Permits  1,395   1,432  1,443   1,442  1,442	1,432</p>
<p> STARTS:    June     May (Prev)     Apr (Prev)  June 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,110   1,082  1,088   1,133  1,116	1,214</p>
<p> -Multiple   342     303    309     350    352	  274</p>
<p> PERMITS    June     May (Prev)     Apr (Prev)  June 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,045   1,053  1,056   1,060  1,060	1,094</p>
<p> -Multiple   350     379    387     382    382	  338</p>
<p>  JUNE STARTS--Pct--Rate    JUNE PERMITS-Pct---Rate</p>
<p> -NorthEast   -6.6   113    -Northeast   5.4   136</p>
<p> -Midwest	0.7   294    -Midwest    -2.0   292</p>
<p> -South	 11.2   683    -South	 0.6   636</p>
<p> -West	   1.1   362    -West	-11.3   331</p>
<p>Actual Starts and Permits, unadjusted in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	 June   May   Apr June96</p>
<p>  Starts     133   134   142   138</p>
<p>  Permits    131   132   137   131</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast June starts at a 1.45 million unit annual rate.</p>
